{"author":"rebar-bridge[bot]","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","data":{"compacted_at":1787162784903773829,"compiled_state":{"alias":"silken-stealthful-narwhal","assignee":null,"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","authorship":{"signed":2,"unsigned":0},"authorship_ledger":[{"content_hash":"132a8c55d8a90a224fcbca1a46d0a6f6f17aea5f4bb485a99b208760886142b1","event_uuid":"deddaa22-92ac-4550-9d28-3d4b123515ff","position":{"commit_sha":"2c6fbd38e872de9ca67c171b5d404b054d67a40f","position":"1787158929772021001-deddaa22-92ac-4550-9d28-3d4b123515ff"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"aab15e1c15e53bd2aa4475e2453fcb4291dd987e0e19ac045353a8fe249ca068","event_uuid":"aca630c2-c882-4ad3-b786-c361c03d4408","position":{"commit_sha":"e5a967e07f8b6dde7c90142ebc08db36d162bb52","position":"1787158934254519001-aca630c2-c882-4ad3-b786-c361c03d4408"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"}],"bridge_alerts":[],"bridge_project":null,"claim_harness":null,"claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":null,"comments":[],"created_at":1787158929772021001,"creation_channel":"cli","deps":[{"link_uuid":"aca630c2-c882-4ad3-b786-c361c03d4408","relation":"discovered_from","target_id":"3199-d739-8804-4746"}],"description":"Latent robustness gap found by the LLM code review of Gerrit 1905 (C4). scripts/gen_config_reference.py::_lifecycle_index() uses dict.setdefault when mapping a canonical schema key to its lifecycle note, so if a single canonical replacement key is ever the target of MORE THAN ONE cfg deprecation alias and/or tombstone, only the first-encountered note survives and the rest are silently dropped from docs/config-reference.md.\n\nNo current collision exists (each cfg replacement key is targeted exactly once in rebar._deprecations.REGISTRY+tombstones()), so today's generated output is correct — this is a defensive fix, not a live bug. Fix: accumulate notes per canonical key (join multiple lifecycle notes) instead of setdefault, and add a held-out test that seeds two deprecations/tombstones pointing at the same replacement and asserts BOTH notes render in that key's row.\n\nAC:\\n- [ ] _lifecycle_index accumulates all lifecycle notes for a canonical key (no silent drop).\\n- [ ] A test seeds a 2-alias collision and asserts both notes appear in the key's config-reference.md row.\\n- [ ] gen --check stays clean; existing oracle still GREEN.","env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","file_impact":[],"file_impact_scope":"undeclared","keyring":[],"managed_refs":[],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":null,"parent_status_uuid":"","plan_review_phase":"planning","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":2,"repos":[],"reverts":[],"status":"open","tags":[],"ticket_id":"b0a5-f5c0-e516-4fdc","ticket_type":"task","title":"Harden gen_config_reference _lifecycle_index against multi-alias canonical-key collisions","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["deddaa22-92ac-4550-9d28-3d4b123515ff","aca630c2-c882-4ad3-b786-c361c03d4408"]},"env_id":"","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1787162784903773829,"uuid":"d1a4742c-df22-44b0-acf9-76baf931c874"}